          "gu_star_dart_gu",
          "gu_shooting_star_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In stellar stones, starlight type Gu are the most commonly seen. Those Gu contain the law of the stars, so the fossil develops markings that resemble shining stars. Among star type Gu, rank one star dart Gu is the most common.",
        "chapters": [
          276
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "stellar-stone-markings",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "A star demon bat shoots countless starlight arrows at Immortal Monkey King Shi Lei. Shi Lei calls them merely rank two star arrow Gu, aside from the high numbers, and his mortal killer move fallen grey cloak makes the arrows vanish on contact. A later wing flap sends over ten thousand star arrows that pierce his iron crown eagle body and leave many wounds that are not deep.",
        "chapters": [
          717
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
